# CropperPreview

`CropperPreview` shows the cropped area of an image at whatever size you give it, live, without drawing to a canvas. It is a standalone component: put it anywhere on the page and point it at a cropper. The preview keeps the crop's aspect ratio, so it fits the crop inside its own box and centers it.

<Example {source} title="CropperPreviewDemo">
	<CropperPreviewDemo />
</Example>

## Usage

There are three ways to tell the preview what to show. When more than one is given, the first in this list wins.

1. **The `cropper` prop.** Pass the value of `bind:this` on a `Cropper` or `FixedCropper`. The preview reads the cropper's reactive state, so it follows every change by itself.

   ```svelte
   <script lang="ts">
   	import { Cropper, CropperPreview, type CropperRef } from 'svelte-advanced-cropper';

   	let cropper: CropperRef | undefined = $state();
   </script>

   <Cropper bind:this={cropper} {src} />
   <CropperPreview {cropper} class="preview" />
   ```

2. **The `update()` export.** Bind the preview and hand it a cropper from a callback, for example `onUpdate={(cropper) => preview?.update(cropper)}`. This mirrors the React recipe, and helps when the preview and the cropper live in different components.

3. **Static props.** Pass `state`, `image` and `transitions` yourself, for example values you saved earlier. `loaded` and `loading` control the fade-in.

Give the preview a size with CSS. It fills its box, and its default background is transparent.

<Admonition type="info" title="Differs from React">

In React, `cropper` takes a ref object (`cropper={cropperRef}`) and the preview only re-renders when its parent does, which is why the React docs drive it with `update()` from `onUpdate`. In Svelte, `cropper` takes the bound instance itself, and the preview updates on its own.

</Admonition>

## Props

| Prop                  | Type                                       | Default                    | Description                                                                                          |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `cropper`             | `CropperPreviewDesiredCropperRef` \| `null` | —                          | The cropper to mirror: the `bind:this` value of a cropper, or any object with the same getters.      |
| `state`               | `CropperState` \| `null`                    | `null`                     | Static mode: the state to show.                                                                       |
| `image`               | `CropperImage` \| `null`                    | `null`                     | Static mode: the image to show.                                                                       |
| `transitions`         | `CropperTransitions` \| `null`              | `null`                     | Static mode: transitions to animate with.                                                             |
| `loaded`              | `boolean`                                  | `true`                     | Static mode: whether the image counts as loaded. The preview fades in when it is.                     |
| `loading`             | `boolean`                                  | `false`                    | Static mode: whether an image is loading.                                                             |
| `class`               | `ClassValue`                               | —                          | Classes for the root element. Upstream's `className`.                                                 |
| `style`               | `string`                                   | —                          | Inline style for the root element.                                                                    |
| `contentClassName`    | `ClassValue`                               | —                          | Classes for the content box, the element sized to the crop's aspect ratio.                            |
| `backgroundComponent` | `Component`                                | `CropperPreviewBackground` | Draws the image. It receives `cropper`, `size` (the content size) and `class`.                       |
| `backgroundProps`     | `Record<string, any>`                      | —                          | Extra props for `backgroundComponent`, spread first.                                                  |
| `backgroundClassName` | `ClassValue`                               | —                          | Classes for the image, next to `advanced-cropper-preview__image`.                                     |
| `boundaryComponent`   | `Component`                                | `StretchableBoundary`      | Measures the available space. It must export `stretchTo()` like [`StretchableBoundary`](/docs/components/StretchableBoundary). |
| `boundaryProps`       | `Record<string, any>`                      | —                          | Extra props for `boundaryComponent`. They can override its `stretchAlgorithm`.                       |
| `boundaryClassName`   | `ClassValue`                               | —                          | Classes for the boundary, next to `advanced-cropper-preview__boundary`.                               |
| `wrapperComponent`    | `Component`                                | `CropperPreviewWrapper`    | The root component. It receives `cropper`, `class`, `style` and a `children` snippet.                 |
| `wrapperProps`        | `Record<string, any>`                      | —                          | Extra props for `wrapperComponent`, spread first.                                                     |

`CropperPreviewDesiredCropperRef` is the part of the cropper the preview reads:

```ts
interface CropperPreviewDesiredCropperRef {
	getState: () => CropperState | null;
	getImage: () => CropperImage | null;
	getTransitions: () => CropperTransitions | null;
	isLoading: () => boolean;
	isLoaded: () => boolean;
}
```

## Exports

Bind the preview with `bind:this` to call these. The bound value has the `CropperPreviewRef` type.

| Export    | Signature                                                      | Description                                                                                                                 |
| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `update`  | <code>(cropper?: CropperPreviewDesiredCropperRef &#124; null) =&gt; void</code>  | Shows the given cropper (or stops showing it, when called without one) and refreshes. The `cropper` prop still wins over it. |
| `refresh` | `() => void`                                                   | Measures the available space again. It runs by itself when the window resizes and when the crop's size changes.             |

Call `refresh()` when the preview's container changes size while the window doesn't.

## CSS classes

| Element      | Classes                                                                                                                              |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Root         | `advanced-cropper-preview`, `cropper-preview-wrapper` (without the `advanced-` prefix, as upstream)                                  |
| Fade         | `cropper-preview-wrapper__fade`, `advanced-cropper-fade`, and `advanced-cropper-fade--visible` once loaded                          |
| Boundary     | `advanced-cropper-boundary`, `advanced-cropper-preview__boundary`                                                                    |
| Content      | `advanced-cropper-preview__content`                                                                                                  |
| Image        | `advanced-cropper-background-image`, `advanced-cropper-preview__image`, and `advanced-cropper-preview__image--visible` with an image |

The package also exports the two default parts, `CropperPreviewWrapper` and `CropperPreviewBackground`, as starting points for your own. See [Preview the result](/docs/guides/recipes#preview-the-result) for more examples.
